# Auto commit & push to dev — Delphi

After completing substantive work in this repo, **commit and push to `dev` without asking**.

Agents work on branch **`dev`** and never push `main`. The hourly Homebase Ship
(`C:\Users\PVProductions\HOMEBASE\scripts\daily-ship.ps1`, every hour on the hour) merges `dev`
into `main` after tests pass; pushing `main` triggers the Vercel production deploy for
**https://delphi.pauloventura.org**.

## When to commit + push

- Bug fixes, features, refactors, or config changes under `agent/web/`, root scripts, docs that ship with the app, or deploy files
- Do **not** commit secrets (`.env.local`, API keys, tokens)
- Do **not** create empty commits

## Workflow (every finished task)

1. `git switch dev` (first time: `git switch -c dev --track origin/dev`)
2. `git status` and `git diff` — stage only files related to the task
3. Readable commit subject (Paulo's changelog in Studio HQ → Builds), 1–2 sentences, focus on why
4. `git add` → `git commit` → `git pull --rebase origin dev` if needed → `git push origin dev`
5. Tell the user: commit hash, that it's on `dev` (playable locally via `npm run dev`, port 3000), and live at the next hourly Homebase Ship
6. Also do the app/game closeout: update Homebase `projects/delphi.md`, rebuild `python scripts/build_index.py`, reply with how to test, and a pasteable Claude prompt. Do not wait to be asked.

Urgent live fix only when Paulo says "ship now" / "push live now":
`powershell -File C:\Users\PVProductions\HOMEBASE\scripts\daily-ship.ps1 -Only DELPHI`

## Remote

- Repo: `https://github.com/paulooventura/DELPHI.git`
- Work branch: `dev` · Live branch: `main` (only the Homebase Ship pushes it)

## Do not

- Push `main`, force-push, amend pushed commits, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks
- Push `.env*` or credential files
- Finish a task with unpushed commits on `dev`
